[obs@atlas .ssh]$ sudo firewall-cmd --zone=work --add-port=8080/tcp --permanent # for scheduler
[obs@atlas .ssh]$ sudo firewall-cmd --zone=work --add-port=80/tcp --permanent  # for controler
success
[obs@atlas .ssh]$ sudo firewall-cmd --reload
success


------
The error [Errno 13] permission denied occurs because, in Linux, ports below 1024 (like Port 80) are Privileged Ports. Only the root user can open them.

Since you are running the script as the user obs (not root), the operating system blocks the request.

Here are the two best ways to fix this without compromising security.
-----
# Forward Port 80 -> 8081 in the 'work' zone
sudo firewall-cmd --zone=work --add-forward-port=port=80:proto=tcp:toport=8081 --permanent

# Open Port 80 itself
sudo firewall-cmd --zone=work --add-port=80/tcp --permanent

# Reload to apply
sudo firewall-cmd --reload
